# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_stoplist_sync.py" "STOPLIST SYNC GATE: PASS" "stoplist sync + domain-verb recall (#365 over-reach fix)" "stoplist sync + domain-verb recall: the #365 BUILTIN/SHORT-NAME stoplist is byte-identical across all 3 single-definer branches in 70_social.sql AND mirrored exactly in backtest_cochange.py STOP; the 9 DOMAIN-INTENT verbs (get/set/add/read/write/parse/decode/encode/load) the #365 stoplist over-reached on are now ABSENT from both (recall-restored); the pure-builtin core (pop/stringify/keys/hasprefix/...) still present; content-free" "stoplist sync + domain-verb recall (RECALL audit r4 2026-06-21): PR #365's import-UNCONFIRMED single-definer BUILTIN stoplist over-reached -- alongside pure language/stdlib method tails (Array.pop, JSON.stringify, dict.keys, strings.HasPrefix, json.NewDecoder/Marshal, fmt.Sprintf, json.dumps) it listed DOMAIN-INTENT verbs get/set/add/read/write/parse/decode/encode/load, which carry real cross-file intent (parse a config, load a model, decode a token, read/write a record); a single un-imported definer of such a name IS a legitimate coupling, so dropping it silently removed real couplings (recall regression). FIX restores the 9 verbs (removed from the stoplist in all 3 SQL branches out_adj/in_adj/calls_h AND the mirrored backtest_cochange STOP) keeping ONLY pure tails. This gate is a lightweight literal-stoplist invariant (no DB): (1) SYNC -- all 3 SQL #365 array literals are the same set, byte-identical to the backtest #365 sub-block (drift either way FAILS); (2) RECALL-RESTORE -- the 9 domain verbs are ABSENT from both stoplists (a future re-add of any FAILS, re-pinning recall); (3) NON-EMPTY -- the pure-builtin core survives in both (an over-correction that guts the list, re-opening the original builtin FP class, also FAILS). The branch's behavioural recall/precision is separately pinned by call_edge_precision / false_coupling_precision / symbol_use_recall / builtin_call_stoplist / cochange_persist staying green. content-free (names only)" 20
